    "title": "State road reopens after former variety store collapsed in Linton - NewsBreak",
    "text": "LINTON, Ind. (WISH) — State Road 59 between State Road 54 and Southeast C Street has reopened after a building that once housed a variety store collapsed on Monday evening in a Greene County city, police said Wednesday. No one was in the downtown Linton building at the intersection of Vincennes Street and State Road 59/Main Street when the brick structure collapsed. The Linton police and fire departments said the debris from the former G.C. Murphy store was being cleared. No injuries were reported. Three or four vehicles near the building were damaged. Linton is a city of about 5,200 residents that’s about a 1-hour, 40-minute drive southwest of downtown Indianapolis.",
